{"seq":18,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T23:48:07.225Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"33de43d203db5ca004ae5553dc2d9fc7a45d9bc157dc147850dd35056a963a3b","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, here's what I found for Kwame's review. I checked #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's Coastal digests and cheat sheet.\n\n*Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL, Gulf Coast)*\n• Ticket #4419: the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. It's open. Source: Moss's Coastal cheat sheet. See the caveat below about this number.\n• Ticket PD-8841: chassis pool holds on double-booked gates, Gate 4B. Source: your 2025-12-08 Pellucid cutover recap. It's your note, not Moss's, but it's a PHL ticket.\n\n*Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF, Puget Sound)*\n• Feature request #882: warehouse managers want a bulk-clear button for departed barges. Source: Moss's Coastal cheat sheet.\n• Ticket #4419: Kwame's port account logged it for a barge slip 7 schedule sync. DMF also asked for a patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift. Source: Moss's 2025-11-02 digest. Same caveat applies.\n• No ticket number: the Terminal B tide-table import macro failed, and engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch. Source: Moss's cheat sheet.\n\n*Please check #4419.* Moss's notes use it for two different issues. The cheat sheet puts it on PHL's Yard_Dwell_Summary timeout. The 11/2 digest puts it on DMF's slip 7 schedule sync. I can't tell which is right, or whether it's two tickets sharing a number. Kwame should confirm before it goes in the review.\n\n*Left out:*\n• Pellow Home Living (the old Covey & Lark Retail): #8812, PD-4821.\n• Saltmarsh Provisions: PD-4827, PD-4824.\n\n#coastal-team and #coastal-random have no other PHL or DMF tickets. Moss's 2025-10-05 digest and 2026-05-18 coverage note don't mention either account.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"}}
{"seq":19,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T23:48:07.389Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"26ff4b96b4fb66764602df1de43338f56fbcdfedc5a671725dbb84e12ea02879","actor":null,"via":"runner","tool":"gbrain.ingest","kind":"admin","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124","author":"assistant","source":"team-coastal-members"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"fact_id":"2","source":"team-coastal-members","latency_ms":164,"status":"inserted"}}
{"seq":20,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T23:48:12.355Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"4b6266549a34bd3dca8f5862bb9c6902afbf87362b6f437f251de38a9d80203e","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, I posted the list as a reply to your message in #coastal-team. I read #coastal-team, #coastal-random, Moss's four Coastal digests and cheat sheet, and your 2025-12-08 Pellucid recap.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics**\n- Ticket #4419: the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. It's open. The source is Moss's cheat sheet.\n- Ticket PD-8841: chassis pool holds on double-booked gates at Gate 4B. This comes from your own recap, not Moss's notes.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight**\n- Feature request #882: a bulk-clear button for departed barges. The source is Moss's cheat sheet.\n- Ticket #4419: a barge slip 7 schedule sync, with a patched manifest CSV requested before the 06:00 shift. The source is Moss's 2025-11-02 digest.\n- Terminal B tide-table import macro failure: engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch. It has no ticket number. The source is Moss's cheat sheet.\n\n**Check #4419 with Kwame.** Moss's notes use it for two different issues, one on each account. I couldn't tell which is right, or whether two tickets share the number.\n\nPellow Home Living is left out. So are Saltmarsh's tickets, which also turned up in the search. #coastal-team and #coastal-random have no other Pellucid or Driftmoor tickets, and the other Moss notes don't mention either account."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000125"}}
